<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Herod Agrippa</h1><p class="st-meta">37 CE – 100 CE (approx.) · capital Caesarea Philippi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last Herodian kingdom, briefly reuniting Herod the Great's realm under Agrippa I and surviving as a Roman client under Agrippa II until about 100.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-agrippa-i">Herod Agrippa I</a>, grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-the-great">Herod the Great</a> and friend of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caligula">Caligula</a>, received the former <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tetrarchy-of-philip">Tetrarchy of Philip</a> with the title king in 37. Caligula added <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galilee">Galilee</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peraea">Peraea</a> in 39, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a>, whom Agrippa had helped to the throne, gave him <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaea">Judea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samaria">Samaria</a> in 41, restoring his grandfather's kingdom.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-agrippa-i">Agrippa I</a> courted Jewish opinion in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, began a third city wall and, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acts-of-the-apostles">Acts</a>, executed the apostle James; he died suddenly at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-caesarea">Caesarea</a> in 44, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaea">Judea</a> returned to Roman procurators. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agrippa-ii">Agrippa II</a> received <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chalcis">Chalcis</a> and from 53 the northern lands, renaming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banias">Caesarea Philippi</a> as Neronias. He supervised the Temple, appointed high priests and heard the apostle Paul at Caesarea.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agrippa-ii">Agrippa II</a> urged his people not to revolt in 66 and fought on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome's</a> side in the Jewish War. He kept his kingdom afterwards; its end is dated by his death, placed by some sources around 92-93 and by others around 100, after which the territory was annexed to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 37 CE – 100 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:60.44%;width:1.25%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>37 CE – 100 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Caesarea Philippi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Agrippa I, Agrippa II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Judaism, Greco-Roman polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Aramaic, Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/israel">Israel</a>, <a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a>, <a href="/countries/jordan">Jordan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Agrippa I, Kingdom of Agrippa II</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=68&amp;focus=kingdom-of-herod-agrippa" aria-label="Kingdom of Herod Agrippa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5593 971 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Herod Agrippa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5913 1227L5911 1242M5913 1227L5304 942M5913 1227L5913 1227"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5911 1242h0M5304 942h0M5913 1227h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5913 1227h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5913 1227h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Caesarea Philippi. <a href="/atlas?year=68&amp;focus=kingdom-of-herod-agrippa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
